**Alternate Path:** Contribute to 2-3 open source projects (fix bugs, add features), practice reading large codebases, and showcase collaborative work on resume for differentiation.

## Example 14
**Decision:** "I'll skip system programming languages like C/C++, only learn JavaScript/Python."

Month 1: Master JavaScript and Python. Build multiple web apps. Never touched C/C++ beyond college labs. Resume shows modern tech stack. Apply to 50 companies, clear many OAs written in preferred languages.

Month 2: Qualcomm interview asks: "Implement this in C++" - struggle with pointers, memory management. "Explain stack vs heap allocation" - vague answer. Nvidia asks about CUDA - requires C++, eliminated. Realize hardware/systems companies need compiled languages.

Month 3: Amazon asks to debug memory leak - don't understand manual memory management coming from garbage-collected languages. Can't explain how Python manages memory internally. Google asks about pointers - rusty from lack of practice.

Month 4: Good offers from web companies but rejected from systems/low-level companies offering higher packages. Samsung, Qualcomm, Intel all require C/C++. Watch batchmate with C++ skills join trading firm at 42 LPA doing low-latency systems.

Month 5: Join web development role at 12 LPA. Content but realize eliminated from entire category of high-paying systems/trading/embedded companies. Colleague mentions quant firms pay 50+ LPA for C++ developers - opportunity cost hitting hard.

Month 6: Decide to learn C++ for off-campus opportunities. Realize starting from scratch when peers already expert. Trading firms like Tower Research, Graviton want C++ - could've applied if prepared. Start competitive C++ but months behind.

**Risk Level:** MEDIUM  
**Root Cause:** Skipping systems languages eliminates entire high-paying categories (trading, systems programming, embedded, gaming) that specifically require C/C++ and offer premium compensation.  
**Alternate Path:** Learn C++ fundamentals alongside web technologies, practice memory management and pointers, solve 50-100 LeetCode problems in C++, and keep systems programming as career option.

## Example 15
