## Example 5: Starting internship search in Month 11 (last month of college year)
**Month 1-10:** Focus on studies and DSA prep for placements. No internship applications.

**Month 11:** Realize internships look good on resume for placements. Frantically apply to 50 companies. Some interest. Interview rounds start.

**Month 11.5:** Get 2 internship offers. But placements start in 2 weeks. Accept one internship (1 month duration) and internship ends right before placements.

**Month 12 (internship):** Work on internship 8 hours/day. Simultaneously, placement prep reduced to 30 mins/day. DSA skills decay.

**Month 12.5:** Internship ends. Placements start. Need to resume DSA. But 1 month gap caused skill decay. First 3 interview attempts mediocre. By Month 13, DSA back to good level. But missed early windows (TCS, Infosys, Amazon).

**Month 14:** Get HCL offer (₹2.8 LPA). Peers without internship but focused on placements got TCS/Infosys (₹3.5 LPA). Internship added ₹5K to offer (internship stipend), but lost opportunity for higher placement.

**Risk Level:** MEDIUM

**Root Cause:** Internship search started too late (Month 11); accepting internship right before placement season created skill decay during a 1-month gap, and missed early company windows.

**Alternate Path:** Apply for internships in Month 6-7 (6 months before placements). Do internship in Month 7-8, finish by Month 8. Resume DSA intensively in Month 9-10. Placements strong.

