## Example 7: Starting a side project in Month 8 before placements
**Month 1-7:** DSA + system design prep. 200 LeetCode problems. 5 system design mocks. Solid foundation.

**Month 8:** Excited: idea for AI recommendation engine. Start building side project. Allocate 10 hours/week. Plus placement interviews start.

**Month 8.5:** Amazon phone screen: strong DSA round. System design: medium (some gaps from distraction). Advanced round scheduled for Month 9.

**Month 9:** Advance round requires deeper system design. But side project deadline looms (want to showcase to investors). Dedicate 20 hours/week to side project. System design prep drops.

**Month 9.5:** Advanced round: weak system design (haven't practiced in 3 weeks). Rejected. Regret project distraction.

**Month 10:** Side project nearly complete. But Amazon rejection stings. Placement now with TCS (₹3.5 LPA).

**Risk Level:** MEDIUM-HIGH

**Root Cause:** Starting a side project in Month 8 (critical interview month) divided attention; system design is skill that decays without practice (3 weeks of no mocks = decay), and interviews couldn't wait for project completion.

**Alternate Path:** Complete DSA + placements (Month 8-10). Start side project in Month 11 (post-placement).

