## Example 19: Requesting CGPA improvement in Month 11 (too late to change grades)
**Month 1-10:** Medium effort on studies. CGPA: 7.2. Realized placements look for 7.5+ CGPA (many companies have this cutoff).

**Month 11:** Placement season. You're not eligible for TCS, Infosys, Amazon (all have 7.5 CGPA minimum). Panic: "Can I improve CGPA?"

**Month 11.5:** Talk to college: grades are finalized. Can't improve now (previous 6 semesters closed). Only current semester (Month 11-12 coursework) counts, but won't be reflected until Month 12.5 (after placements).

**Month 12:** You're CGPA-ineligible for most campus drives. Only non-CGPA companies remain: HCL (hire anyone), local companies. Get HCL offer (₹2.8 LPA).

**Result:** CGPA cutoff locked you out. Peers with 7.5+ CGPA got TCS/Infosys (₹3.5 LPA), regardless of DSA skill.

**Risk Level:** HIGH

**Root Cause:** Maintaining low CGPA (7.2) through Month 10 meant no time to improve before CGPA cutoffs apply; companies finalize cutoff in Month 8-9, and previous semesters can't be retaken.

**Alternate Path:** Maintain 7.5+ CGPA from the start (Year 1). CGPA is accumulated score; once low, hard to recover. Consistent 8+ GPA per semester ensures eligibility.

