## Example 23: Waiting for "perfect time" to start placements prep (eternal procrastination)
**Month 1:** "I'll start placements prep next month, want to enjoy college first."

**Month 2:** "Still adjusting to college, I'll start seriously in Month 3."

**Month 3:** "Midterm exams this month, next month for sure."

**Month 4:** "Summer break coming, I'll do placements prep over summer."

**Month 5:** Summer break. "Summer is too hot, I'll start in Month 6 when college resumes."

**Month 6:** "Just started college, getting settled. I'll start in Month 7."

**Month 7:** "Month 8 is better, less workload."

**Month 8:** "Oh wait, placements start THIS month. I need to start NOW."

