**Month 12:** Annual review: get 10% hike. New salary: ₹5.28 LPA. Regret: if negotiated at offer (Month 5), could have gotten ₹5.2+ LPA immediately.

**Result:** Cost of not negotiating at offer time: ₹4800 (difference between accepting at ₹4.8 and negotiating to ₹5.2).

**Risk Level:** MEDIUM

**Root Cause:** Accepting offer without negotiating at offer-time (when leverage is high) meant losing negotiation opportunity; once hired, salary is fixed until annual review.

**Alternate Path:** At offer-time (Month 5), negotiate: "Can we improve to ₹5.2 LPA?" Likely yes (candidate is valuable, negotiation expected). Accept at higher salary immediately.

