Month 5: Phonepe and Razorpay interviews—you're more accurate now but months of blog-learning created misconceptions you're still unlearning. Peers who read docs first have cleaner mental models.
Month 6: You get Razorpay at 21 LPA. First code review, you cite a blog. Senior dev asks "Did you check the docs?" You realize docs are source of truth, blogs are interpretation. You prioritize official sources now, blogs for discovery only.

**Risk Level:** MEDIUM  
**Root Cause:** Learning primarily from blogs instead of official documentation created opinionated, sometimes incorrect, incomplete knowledge without foundational understanding.  
**Alternate Path:** Use blogs for discovering topics; always verify with official docs; read RFCs/specs for deep understanding; docs first, blogs for perspectives.


